A server script over 50 KB (ssl.diagnostics.maxScriptBytes, default
51,200 bytes) reports diag.script_size_ceiling once, a warning on line 1,
in the default profile (issue #358). Most of its size is an HTML email
template in a :REGION block, which counts like any other text: the size
is every byte of the file, line endings included. Its few code lines stay
under the script_size_review triggers.
-- input.ssl --
/* Sends the weekly status summary by email;
:PARAMETERS sRecipient;
:DECLARE oEmail, sBody;

sBody := GetRegion("SummaryTemplate");
oEmail := Email{};
oEmail:Subject := "Weekly status summary";
oEmail:Body := sBody;
oEmail:AddRecipient(sRecipient);
:RETURN oEmail:Send();

:REGION SummaryTemplate;
<html><body><table class="summary">
<tr class="row-001"><td class="label">Status table 001</td><td class="value">{{count_001}}</td><td class="note">Counts every sample in the table that is still awaiting review at the end of the week, grouped by the owning laboratory and the reviewer assigned to it.</td><td class="link"><a href="{{base_url}}/status/001">Open the table</a></td></tr>
